description:
New bytecodes were introduced by #1831, which breaks the shared cache compatibility. The shared cache generation was not increased. A simple test case is:
class Test { public static boolean doPrint() {
 return true;
 }
 public static void main(String args[]) { if (doPrint()) {
 System.out.println("Hello, World"); }
 } } I stored the class to the shared cache using an old JVM before #1831. java -Xshareclasses:name=Cache1 Test
Hello, World
Then startup the shared cache again using the newest JVM (with -Xshareclasses:readonly). `java -Xshareclasses:name=Cache1,readonly Test`
I get:
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.VerifyError: JVMVRFY012 stack shape inconsistent; class=Test, method=doPrint()Z, pc=1
Exception Details:
 Location:
 Test.doPrint()Z @1: JBireturn
 Reason:
 Type integer (current frame, stack[0]) is not assignable to integer
 Current Frame:
 bci: @1
 flags: { }
 locals: { }
 stack: { integer }
 at java.lang.J9VMInternals.prepareClassImpl(Native Method)
 at java.lang.J9VMInternals.prepare(J9VMInternals.java:304)
 at java.lang.Class.getMethodHelper(Class.java:1243)
 at java.lang.Class.getMethod(Class.java:1187)
 at sun.launcher.LauncherHelper.validateMainClass(LauncherHelper.java:556)
 at sun.launcher.LauncherHelper.checkAndLoadMain(LauncherHelper.java:538)

