description:
We’ve defined 4 `J9ClassLoader` fields in `J9JavaVM`:
 struct J9ClassLoader* systemClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader *platformClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader* extensionClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader* applicationClassLoader;
and I believe there should only be 3 with `platformClassLoader` and `extensionClassLoader` always pointing at the same loader.
we can remove platformClassLoader and replace the usage with extensionClassLoader. It's only used in JVM_DefineModule()

text:
Bug Title: Have the right 3 J9ClassLoaders pointers in J9JavaVM
Bug Description: We’ve defined 4 `J9ClassLoader` fields in `J9JavaVM`:
 struct J9ClassLoader* systemClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader *platformClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader* extensionClassLoader;
 struct J9ClassLoader* applicationClassLoader;
and I believe there should only be 3 with `platformClassLoader` and `extensionClassLoader` always pointing at the same loader.
we can remove platformClassLoader and replace the usage with extensionClassLoader. It's only used in JVM_DefineModule()

description:
Java -version output
openjdk version "11.0.7" 2020-04-14
OpenJDK Runtime Environment AdoptOpenJDK (build 11.0.7+8-202003231120)
Eclipse OpenJ9 VM AdoptOpenJDK (build master-51420720e, JRE 11 Linux amd64-64-Bit Compressed References 20200323_542 (JIT enabled, AOT enabled)
OpenJ9 - 51420720e
OMR - 24a81ac88
JCL - d1ca0ebebe based on jdk-11.0.7+8)
Summary of problem
The JVM is failing to set the module on some `java.lang.Class` objects. The function `getModule()` in `java.lang.Class` should not return null, but there are classes with a null module. I found this by writing a JVMTI agent which uses the VMDeath handle to process all loaded classes in the course of calling `getResource` on some of these classes I get an internal NPE from `getResource` due to a null module.
Diagnostic files
Some source code to generate an agent to provoke the problem:
JNIEXPORT
void JNICALL
VMDeath(jvmtiEnv *jvmti, JNIEnv* env)
{
 jvmtiError err;
 printf("\nStart Shutdown Processing\n");
 jint classCount = 0;
 jclass *clazzItr;
 if (jvmti->GetLoadedClasses(&classCount, &clazzItr) != 0)
 return;
 // call getModule using JNI on clazzItr here - some will have a null result which should not happen
}
JNIEXPORT jint JNICALL
Agent_OnLoad(JavaVM *vm, char *options, void *reserved) {
 jvmtiEnv *jvmti;
 //Get JVMTI environment
 jint result = vm->GetEnv((void**)&jvmti, JVMTI_VERSION_1_2);
 if(result != 0){
 return JNI_FALSE;
 }
 jvmti->SetEventNotificationMode(JVMTI_ENABLE, JVMTI_EVENT_VM_DEATH, NULL);
 jvmtiEventCallbacks callbacks;
 (void)memset(&callbacks, 0, sizeof(callbacks));
 callbacks.VMDeath = &VMDeath;
 jvmti->SetEventCallbacks(&callbacks, (jint)sizeof(callbacks));
 printf("\nSizeAgent Loaded\n");
 return JNI_OK;
}

