description:
I noticed that our JVMTI agent sometimes did not properly shutdown when used together with IBM/OpenJ9 JVM.
I reproduced the problem with a simple JVMTI agent that just registers a VMDeath callback and then sleep for a second there before printing a message.
 static void VMDeath(jvmtiEnv *jvmti_env, JNIEnv* jni_env) {
 fprintf(stderr, "Enter VMDeath\n");
 std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(1000));
 fprintf(stderr, "Exit VMDeath\n");
 }
[IncompleteVmDeathReproducer.zip](
VMDeath callback is not run to completion each time I run this agent together with the following Java code:
 public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
 final CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(1);
 Thread thread = new Thread() {
 public void run() {
 // Trigger VMDeath in main thread
 latch.countDown();
 try {
 Thread.sleep(100);
 } catch (InterruptedException e) {
 e.printStackTrace();
 }
 // Before VMDeath completes call System.exit
 System.exit(0);
 }
 };
 thread.setDaemon(true);
 thread.start();
 latch.await();
 }
This just prints
 Enter VMDeath
before process dies.
With Hotspot JVM I get the expected result:
 Enter VMDeath
 Exit VMDeath

