- Java Debug Wire Protocol (Reference Implementation) version 11.0
- JVM Debug Interface version 11.0
- JVM version 11.0.7 (Eclipse OpenJ9 VM, JRE 11 Windows 10 amd64-64-Bit Compressed References 20200422_551 (JIT enabled, AOT enabled)
- OpenJ9 - 05fa2d361
- OMR - d4365f371
- JCL - 838028fc9d based on jdk-11.0.7+10)
Summary of problem
I have an application that connects to a remove JVM using JDI. The remove JVM is running OpenJ9. As part of invoking a method with a varargs signature, JDI calls VisibleClasses on the class loader of the declaring type of the method. The result is:
com.sun.jdi.ClassNotLoadedException: Class java.lang.Object[] not loaded
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.ClassLoaderReferenceImpl.findType(ClassLoaderReferenceImpl.java:107)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.ReferenceTypeImpl.findType(ReferenceTypeImpl.java:1153)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.MethodImpl.argumentType(MethodImpl.java:162)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.MethodImpl.argumentTypes(MethodImpl.java:169)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.MethodImpl.handleVarArgs(MethodImpl.java:301)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.MethodImpl.validateAndPrepareArgumentsForInvoke(MethodImpl.java:366)
 at com.sun.tools.jdi.ObjectReferenceImpl.invokeMethod(ObjectReferenceImpl.java:407)
I have tried printing visible classes just before invoking the the method, and the list contains a number of `java.lang` classes (and interfaces, see below) including `java.lang.Object` but not `java.lang.Object[]`. In fact, the list contains no array types at all:
