description:
Some time back, I [proposed ]( that the Java preprocessor should support numeric comparisons, in particular expressions like
/*[IF JAVA_SPEC_VERSION >= 11]*/
That would reduce the number of configurations required in `jpp_configuration.xml`, and would eliminate the need to add a new configurations every six months (e.g. `JAVA16` was added recently and before March we would need to add `JAVA17`).
Some conditions would read more naturally: consider this example from [`String.java`](
/*[IF Java12 & !Java13]*/
which could be replace by:
/*[IF JAVA_SPEC_VERSION == 12]*/

