/*[IF JAVA_SPEC_VERSION == 12]*/

description:
The following test displays intermittent crashes or hangs running with the option `-XX:+EnableValhalla`. The problem appears to be some sort of interaction between `monitorenter`/`monitorexit` and `acmp` expansion in lower trees in JIT-compiled trees for `ConcurrentHashMap.putVal`.
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
public class TestACMP {
 public static final void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
 final ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer>();
 final int nthreads = 256;
 final int nvals = 1024;
 Thread[] tarr = new Thread[nthreads];
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 final int tnum = i;
 tarr[i] = new Thread() {
 public void run() {
 for (int j = 0; j < nvals; j++) {
 map.put(Integer.valueOf(j), Integer.valueOf(j));
 }
 };
 };
 }
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 tarr[i].start();
 }
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 tarr[i].join();
 }
 }
}
Run with `-Xjit:count=1,disableAsyncCompilation`

text:
Bug Title: Intermittent crashes or hangs in JIT compiled code using ConcurrentHashMap with -XX:+EnableValhalla
Bug Description: The following test displays intermittent crashes or hangs running with the option `-XX:+EnableValhalla`. The problem appears to be some sort of interaction between `monitorenter`/`monitorexit` and `acmp` expansion in lower trees in JIT-compiled trees for `ConcurrentHashMap.putVal`.
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
public class TestACMP {
 public static final void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
 final ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<Integer, Integer>();
 final int nthreads = 256;
 final int nvals = 1024;
 Thread[] tarr = new Thread[nthreads];
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 final int tnum = i;
 tarr[i] = new Thread() {
 public void run() {
 for (int j = 0; j < nvals; j++) {
 map.put(Integer.valueOf(j), Integer.valueOf(j));
 }
 };
 };
 }
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 tarr[i].start();
 }
 for (int i = 0; i < tarr.length; i++) {
 tarr[i].join();
 }
 }
}
Run with `-Xjit:count=1,disableAsyncCompilation`

