description:
Error
`IllegalStateException` is thrown for `MutableCallSite` when OJDK MHs are enabled in OpenJ9.
**Java16 doc** for `MutableCallSite`: Exception in thread "main" java.lang.IllegalStateException: uninitialized call site
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.CallSite.uninitializedCallSite(CallSite.java:261)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.LambdaForm$DMH/<hex>.invokeStatic(LambdaForm$DMH)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.LambdaForm$MH/<hex>.invoke(LambdaForm$MH)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.LambdaForm$MH/<hex>.invoke(LambdaForm$MH)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.LambdaForm$MH/<hex>.invokeExact_MT(LambdaForm$MH)
 at MethodHandleTest.main(MethodHandleTest.java:)
 Micro-test
import static java.lang.invoke.MethodHandles.*;
import static java.lang.invoke.MethodType.*;
import java.lang.invoke.*;
public class MethodHandleTest {
 public static void main(String[] args) throws Throwable {
 MethodType methodType = MethodType.methodType(String.class);
 MutableCallSite mutableCallSite = new MutableCallSite(methodType);
 MethodHandle methodHandle = mutableCallSite.dynamicInvoker();
 Lookup lkup = MethodHandles.publicLookup();
 MethodHandle mhLowerCase = lkup.findVirtual(String.class, "toLowerCase", methodType);
 MethodHandle convertToLowerCase = MethodHandles.filterReturnValue(methodHandle, mhLowerCase);
 mutableCallSite.setTarget(MethodHandles.constant(String.class, "TestString"));
 String lowerCaseStr = (String)convertToLowerCase.invokeExact(); // IllegalStateException thrown from here
 if (lowerCaseStr.equals("teststring")) {
 System.out.println("pass: " + lowerCaseStr);
 } else {
 System.out.println("fail: " + lowerCaseStr);
 }
 }
}
 Steps to build an OpenJ9 JDK with OJDK MHs enabled
Refer to #11458.

