description:
An issue occurs with the following test
protected static NodeInterface getAnonInvoker() throws IllegalAccessException, IOException, InstantiationException {
 String resource = NodeClass.class.getName().replace('.', '/') + ".class";
 InputStream classFile = j9vm.test.invoker.NodeClass.class.getClassLoader().getResourceAsStream(resource);
 byte[] classFileBytes = new byte[classFile.available()];
 classFile.read(classFileBytes);
 Unsafe unsafe = getUnsafeInstance();
 NodeInterface anonInvoker = (NodeInterface)unsafe.defineAnonymousClass(NodeInterface.class, classFileBytes, null).newInstance();
 return anonInvoker;
 }
NodeClass is defined as:
class j9vm/test/invoker/NodeClass
 implements j9vm/test/invoker/NodeInterface
 version 52:0
{
public Method <init>:"()V"
 stack 1 locals 2
{
 aload_0;
 invokespecial Method java/lang/Object."<init>":"()V";
 return;
}
public Method callRootIdentity:"(Ljava/lang/Object;)Ljava/lang/Boolean;" stack 2 locals 3
{
 /* aload_0 replaced with aload_1 change receiver */
 aload 1;
 invokespecial InterfaceMethod j9vm/test/invoker/Root.identity:"()Ljava/lang/Boolean;";
 areturn;
}
}
When one attempts to replace defineAnonClass with defineHidden class.
The failure is:
java.lang.NoClassDefFoundError: j9vm.test.invoker.NodeClass.<hex>
 at java.base/java.lang.ClassLoader.defineClassInternal(ClassLoader.java:529)
 at java.base/java.lang.Access.defineClass(Access.java:336)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.MethodHandles$Lookup$ClassDefiner.defineClass(MethodHandles.java:2445)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.MethodHandles$Lookup$ClassDefiner.defineClassAsLookup(MethodHandles.java:2426)
 at java.base/java.lang.invoke.MethodHandles$Lookup.defineHiddenClass(MethodHandles.java:2133)
 at org.openj9.test.access.UnsafeClasses.defineAnonOrHiddenClass(UnsafeClasses.java:47)
 at j9vm.test.invoker.InvokeSpecialInsideInterface.getAnonInvoker(InvokeSpecialInsideInterface.java:132)
 at j9vm.test.invoker.InvokeSpecialInsideInterface.invokeSpecialInsideInterface(InvokeSpecialInsideInterface.java:77)
 at java.base/jdk.internal.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke0(Native Method)
 at java.base/jdk.internal.reflect.NativeMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(NativeMethodAccessorImpl.java:77)
 at java.base/jdk.internal.reflect.DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.invoke(DelegatingMethodAccessorImpl.java:43)
 at java.base/java.lang.reflect.Method.invoke(Method.java:568)
 at org.testng.internal.MethodInvocationHelper.invokeMethod(MethodInvocationHelper.java:124)
 at org.testng.internal.Invoker.invokeMethod(Invoker.java:580)
 at org.testng.internal.Invoker.invokeTestMethod(Invoker.java:716)
 at org.testng.internal.Invoker.invokeTestMethods(Invoker.java:988)
 at org.testng.internal.TestMethodWorker.invokeTestMethods(TestMethodWorker.java:125)
 at org.testng.internal.TestMethodWorker.run(TestMethodWorker.java:109)
 at org.testng.TestRunner.privateRun(TestRunner.java:648)
 at org.testng.TestRunner.run(TestRunner.java:505)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunner.runTest(SuiteRunner.java:455)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunner.runSequentially(SuiteRunner.java:450)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunner.privateRun(SuiteRunner.java:415)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunner.run(SuiteRunner.java:364)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunnerWorker.runSuite(SuiteRunnerWorker.java:52)
 at org.testng.SuiteRunnerWorker.run(SuiteRunnerWorker.java:84)
 at org.testng.TestNG.runSuitesSequentially(TestNG.java:1208)
 at org.testng.TestNG.runSuitesLocally(TestNG.java:1137)
 at org.testng.TestNG.runSuites(TestNG.java:1049)
 at org.testng.TestNG.run(TestNG.java:1017)
 at org.testng.TestNG.privateMain(TestNG.java:1354)
 at org.testng.TestNG.main(TestNG.java:1323)
Caused by: java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: j9vm.test.invoker.NodeClass.<hex>
 at java.base/jdk.internal.loader.BuiltinClassLoader.loadClass(BuiltinClassLoader.java:827)
 at java.base/jdk.internal.loader.ClassLoaders$AppClassLoader.loadClass(ClassLoaders.java:188)
 at java.base/java.lang.ClassLoader.loadClass(ClassLoader.java:1113)
 at java.base/java.lang.ClassLoader.defineClassImpl1(Native Method)
 ... 32 more
The VM is looking for a class named `j9vm.test.invoker.NodeClass.<hex>` but it should really be looking for `j9vm.test.invoker.NodeClass/<hex>`
So there is an issue with the self reference in the constantPool. I recommend starting the investigation by looking at We need to patch all self references in the constantPool because the class (hidden/anon) are not searchable. Failure to do this properly may be the cause of the NCDFE.

