description:
Java -version output
Eclipse OpenJ9 VM 17.0.0.0-m1 (build openj9-0.28.0-m2, JRE 17 Windows 10 amd64-64-Bit Compressed References 20210916_31 (JIT enabled, AOT enabled)
Summary of problem
Consider the following small program:
package tests;
import java.net.InetAddress;
import java.net.UnknownHostException;
public class TestCompactString {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 try {
 String hostName = InetAddress.getLocalHost().getHostName();
 System.out.println( "hostName="+hostName );
 String hostName2=new StringBuilder(hostName).append(".localdomain").toString();
 System.out.println( "hostName2="+hostName2 );
 boolean testOK=hostName2.startsWith(hostName);
 System.out.println( "hostName2.startsWith(hostName) returned "+testOK );
 } catch (UnknownHostException e) {
 e.printStackTrace();
 }
 }
}
Run it using IBM Semeru 17 Milestone 2:
- Once with standard options:
 `java.exe tests\TestCompactString.java`
 and see the result, which is expected:
 `hostName=LP5-LAI-ACM`
 `hostName2=LP5-LAI-ACM.localdomain`
 `hostName2.startsWith(hostname) returned true`
- Once with -XX:+CompactStrings option:
 `java.exe -XX:+CompactStrings tests\TestCompactString.java`
 and see the result, which is failing:
 `hostName=LP5-LAI-ACM`
 `hostName2=LP5-LAI-ACM.localdomain`
 `hostName2.startsWith(hostname) returned false`
It looks like InetAddress.getLocalHost() isn't compatible with -XX:+CompactStrings.
The same scenario works well with Adoptium JDK 17.
Would you please check this ?
Kind regards,
Alexandre

