description:
Description:
I use the try-catch statement to catch an `IllegalStateException` object named `ise`. Then I call the `getCause` method to perform a Cause check and find that it cannot find the Cause object (Testcase1 below). However, HotSpot returned t2.
And when I define the Cause object of `ise` directly and then use `getCause` to check it, I find that it can find the Cause object (Testcase2 below).
It seems that the try-catch statement has an effect on the `IllegalStateException` object calling the `getCause` method, is this an issue with the implementation of OpenJ9?
By the way, if you need more information about this, please contact me.
 Environment：
Ubuntu 18.04 x86_64
 JVM Information:
 jdk8:
openjdk version "1.8.0_332-internal"
OpenJDK Runtime Environment (build 1.8.0_332-internal-_2022_02_17_10_23-b00)
Eclipse OpenJ9 VM (build master-39c490eaf, JRE 1.8.0 Linux amd64-64-Bit Compressed References 20220217_000000 (JIT enabled, AOT enabled)
OpenJ9 - 39c490eaf
OMR - b63287860
JCL - 301202f49f based on jdk8u332-b02)
 jdk11:
openjdk version "11.0.15-internal" 2022-04-19
