description:
The following is used for mismatch operations in MemoryAccessAPIs. The JDK supplies a java implementation which is very slow. We are seeing test failures due to timeouts as a result of this, This API takes two arrays (of the same type) and compares each elements until there is a mismatch. This operation is can be applied to all primitive array types, the `log2ArrayIndexScale` denotes which type it is.
class jdk.internal.util.ArraySupport {
 @IntrinsicCandidate
 public static int vectorizedMismatch(Object a, long aOffset, Object b, long bOffset, int length, int log2ArrayIndexScale) }

text:
Bug Title: Panama MemoryAccessAPI: Add jit intrinsic support for vectorizedMismatch
Bug Description: The following is used for mismatch operations in MemoryAccessAPIs. The JDK supplies a java implementation which is very slow. We are seeing test failures due to timeouts as a result of this, This API takes two arrays (of the same type) and compares each elements until there is a mismatch. This operation is can be applied to all primitive array types, the `log2ArrayIndexScale` denotes which type it is.
class jdk.internal.util.ArraySupport {
 @IntrinsicCandidate
 public static int vectorizedMismatch(Object a, long aOffset, Object b, long bOffset, int length, int log2ArrayIndexScale) }

