**Description**
As the following test case shows, when I try to clear the list content of `ManagementFactory.getRuntimeMXBean().getInputArguments()`, no error is thrown. However, in HotSpot, any attempts to invoke `clear()` or modify the returned list will result in an error being thrown. **Testcase**
import java.lang.management.ManagementFactory;
import java.util.List;
public class MyJVMTest {
 public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
 List<String> l1 = ManagementFactory.getRuntimeMXBean().getInputArguments();
 l1.clear();
 // l1.add("a");
 // An add operator is also allowed. }
}
**Output of OpenJ9**
**Output of HotSpot**
Exception in thread "main" java.lang.UnsupportedOperationException
 at java.util.Collections$UnmodifiableCollection.add(Collections.java:1057)
 at MyJVMTest.main(MyJVMTest.java:7)
